een  going on in the country in the last few  years  uh we  asked you or a caller asked you to talk  about the  labels you would  put on the  yandi government when he was in power  could you do the same thing for the  pinochet government would you call him a  right extreme right authoritarian or  what  i guess authoritarian is maybe the best  way to call him  he is  a military man president pinochet  he is still the commander-in-chief of  the army  in fact according to the constitution  he will  continue to be commander-in-chief of the  army if the no vote wins this is sort of  a paradoxical situation he loses the  election that is coming up  he would still continue for at least  four more years commander chief of the  army he's very much of a military man  i don't think he has too much sympathy  for democratic politics  and as such i guess authoritarian is the  best  label  encino california go ahead please yes  thank you i just want to make a  quick comment i was recently in chile  i'm a businessman and it was when i was  there  after several meetings with some  outstanding individuals in the academic  community  and some very aggressive young business  people and i'm in the communication  business and i won't mention names or  anything i noticed that i wasn't alone  after my second meeting  my driver was stopped in question  i think my phones were tapped um i even  had a visit an impromptu visit from some  individual who i suspect was in the  central intelligence agency  i think in chile now today is still  repressive there's still a great deal of  paranoia but as i agree with the  gentleman uh they're more discreet far  more uh i think secretive about who they  target and who they may  say whisk off in the night so to speak  things have changed but uh not a heck of  a lot i just want to hang up and listen  to this guy caller while you're still on  the line uh did you feel in any personal  peril while you were in chile no i  didn't feel any personal peril at all 