ts i think there is uh  a legitimate political risk issue  in relationship to chile uh  in the next few years  particularly if the yes uh is  confirmed and if pinochet is in power  for another eight years  i do foresee uh considerable  confrontation and polarization in the  country and this could  lead to a situation where the business  climate deteriorates rather  significantly  but my impression has been that  u.s businessmen for the most part who  have opted for investing in chile  have been relatively pleased with  the kinds of returns that they've been  getting  we'll take our last call from hampton  virginia go ahead please  um yes basically my question is even if  pinochet is defeated in this election  according to the 1980 uh  constitution he's become a senator for  life playing a key role in appointing  other members in a new 36-man senate so  basically  he's never  actually going to lose his control in  politics is he  uh  the caller is right that the  constitution  prescribes several roles for pinochet  even if he loses  the election not only will he  be a senator for life as  commander-in-chief of the army which he  would not give up he would also be a  member of the national security council  which is a body that is envisioned in  the chilean constitution that has a  right to admonish  any other  body in the  in the chilean institutional framework  including the congress or the president  if it feels that the president or the  congress or whatever  body is being admonished is violating  national securities and this is a very  important  role in the sense that pinochet has  safeguarded for himself however i really  do feel that if the no vote wins in  chile  even if pinochet  tries to remain as a senator  and particularly if after the no vote  wins the opposition is able to win the  presidency and a majority in the  congress the chilean political situation  will change such that there really won't  be a role anymore for somebody like  president pinochet 